@startuml
skinparam style strictuml

' --- CSS Style Block (replaces skinparam ParticipantPadding & BoxPadding) ---
<style>
participant {
    Padding: 10
}
box {
    Padding: 10
}
</style>

actor "Client / Browser" as Browser
box "Go Web Application (Gin)" #F0F0F0
    participant "Security / CSRF / Auth\nMiddleware" as MW
    participant "Handlers & Services\n(Web / API)" as Handler
    participant "R2 Client\n(AWS SDK v2)" as R2Client
end box
database "PostgreSQL\n(Users & Sessions)" as DB
participant "Cloudflare R2\n(Private Storage)" as R2

== 1. Authentication & Token Issuance (Login Flow) ==

Browser -> MW: POST /web/login (Credentials + CSRF Header/Field)
activate MW
MW -> DB: Validate credentials & check active user
activate DB
DB --> MW: User verified
deactivate DB

MW -> DB: Insert session row (jti, user_id, user_agent, client_ip)
MW -> MW: Generate short-lived Access JWT (15m)\n& long-lived Refresh JWT with 'jti' (7d)\nRotate CSRF Token
MW --> Browser: 200/302 OK\nSet-Cookie: auth_token (HttpOnly, Secure)\nSet-Cookie: refresh_token (HttpOnly, Secure)\nSet-Cookie: csrf_token (Readable)
deactivate MW


== 2. Authorization & Silent Refresh Flow ==

Browser -> MW: GET /web/me (Request protected resource)
activate MW
alt Valid Access Token Present
    MW -> MW: Verify Access JWT (stateless)
else Access Token Expired, Valid Refresh Token Present
    MW -> DB: Check SessionService.IsActive(jti)
    activate DB
    DB --> MW: Session active & unrevoked
    deactivate DB
    MW -> MW: Mint fresh Access JWT
    MW -> Browser: Set-Cookie: auth_token (New Access Token)
end

MW -> MW: Enforce RequireRole() check
MW -> Handler: Pass request context (Claims)
deactivate MW

== 3. Private Asset Fetching (Presigned URL) ==

activate Handler
Handler -> R2Client: PresignGetObject(imageKey, 15m)
activate R2Client
R2Client -> R2Client: Sign S3 GET Request using R2 Secret
R2Client --> Handler: Return Presigned R2 URL
deactivate R2Client

Handler --> Browser: 200 OK (Render HTML with <img src="presigned-url">)
deactivate Handler

Browser -> R2: GET presigned-url (Direct download, no app auth header)
activate R2
R2 --> Browser: 200 OK (Return Image Bytes)
deactivate R2

== 4. Revocation Flow (Logout / Role Change) ==

Browser -> MW: POST /web/logout (or Admin updates role)
activate MW
MW -> DB: Revoke session(s) in 'sessions' table (set revoked_at)
MW --> Browser: Clear auth_token, refresh_token, & csrf_token cookies
deactivate MW

@enduml